# Rust build artifact
target
.ryo

# Local scratch: task workspace, git worktrees
workspace
.worktrees

# What this repository tells an agent is AGENTS.md, at the root, under the name
# other coding agents read. Claude Code reads CLAUDE.md instead, so the one
# tracked file under .claude/ is a symlink pointing back at AGENTS.md — the
# instructions live in one place and load without anyone wiring them up. The
# rest of .claude/ is Claude Code's working directory on a machine (local
# settings, local memory, plugin caches, session state) and is not this
# repository's to carry; the pattern is `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`
# because git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
# /CLAUDE.md is ignored for the same reason: a checkout that cannot make the
# symlink writes one there by hand, and it is that person's file. Everything a
# plugin can carry — agents, skills, commands, hooks — is installed from the
# marketplace declared in .claude-plugin/marketplace.json, whose plugin sources
# sit in ./plugins, rather than cloned.
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
/CLAUDE.md

